pomo (1.7.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: arrow-key + Enter in the menu now works on every item, not just
    the session entries — Enter on Help/Stats/Customize durations/Cycle
    theme runs the action instead of silently returning to a frozen
    timer. run_timer treats any unexpected menu result as "back", so the
    timer can no longer get stuck paused.

 -- Yapidev <yapidev@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:29:39 +0700

pomo (1.7.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Timer screen shows cycle progress (●●○○) toward the long break.
  * Menu: arrow-key navigation (↑/↓ + Enter) alongside the direct keys,
    and the currently running session is marked "(active)".
  * Between sessions: new m (menu — pick any session), t (stats) and
    d (customize durations) shortcuts; quitting from the timer now asks
    for confirmation first.
  * The in-TUI stats overlay (t) shows the same today + 7-day chart as
    "pomo stats"; fixed its "Today" section always showing zeros.
  * Small terminals: the "too small" notice no longer flickers.

 -- Yapidev <yapidev@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:04:46 +0700

pomo (1.6.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Session-specific sounds: separate sounds for focus and break end
    (FOCUS_SOUND/BREAK_SOUND in pomo.conf, played via paplay/aplay with
    a bell fallback).
  * "pomo" without arguments now asks for confirmation before starting
    a focus session.

 -- Yapidev <yapidev@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 07:30:00 +0700

pomo (1.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Config file pomo.conf for durations and the NOTIFY_CMD hook.
  * "pomo status" one-line output for status bars (tmux/waybar), with
    --json for status-bar styling.
  * "pomo resume" continues a session interrupted by a closed terminal
    or a crash.
  * build-deb.sh now derives the package version from POMO_VERSION in
    the script itself, so the .deb label always matches.

 -- Yapidev <yapidev@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:28:40 +0700

pomo (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release of pomo, a pomodoro timer TUI in pure Bash.
  * Large block-character countdown, progress bar, automatic focus/break
    cycle, desktop notifications and session statistics.

